Progress: **35% → 45% next goal**
Your current iOS app is a strong visual prototype, but not yet production-structured. The biggest fix is to stop treating `Core` as a dumping ground.

Right now, your `Core` has:

```text
Core/
  AppSession.swift
  ScubaAPI.swift
  ScubaModels.swift
  ScubaTheme.swift
```

That means one folder is handling:

```text
auth session
token storage
networking
API endpoints
DTOs
domain models
mapping
theme/design system
shared UI components
```

That works early, but becomes painful fast.

Your broader repo already has a backend/mobile split, with backend in `app` and mobile client generation in `mobile/src/api/generated` for Expo/OpenAPI work.  Since this uploaded project is native SwiftUI, I would place it clearly as either `ios/` or `mobile-ios/` so it does not get confused with the Expo mobile app.

## The structure I’d move toward

Use **vertical feature modules** plus a small technical core.

```text
scuba-pal/
  app/                         # Spring Boot backend
  mobile/                      # Expo React Native app, if still used
  ios/                         # Native SwiftUI app
    ScubaPal/
      App/
        ScubaPalApp.swift
        RootView.swift
        AppEnvironment.swift

      Core/
        Networking/
